     "claim": "**The parabolic subgroup.** $W_J=\\langle J\\rangle=\\langle s_1\\rangle=\\{1,s_1\\}$: the definition of $W_J$ as the subgroup generated by $J$ is [F5] and its identity with $\\langle s_1\\rangle$ is immediate for $J=\\{s_1\\}$ [F2]; the relator $s_1^2$ of the presentation gives $s_1^2=1$ [F5], so $\\langle s_1\\rangle\\subseteq\\{1,s_1\\}$, and $s_1\\ne1$ because $\\ell(s_1)=1$ [F6], so $\\langle s_1\\rangle$ has the two distinct elements $1,s_1$; it is a group of order $2$, hence isomorphic to $S_2$.",
     "step": "1.1",
     "inputs": [
      "F5",
      "F2",
      "F6"
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "1.2",
     "claim": "**The right cosets.** The right cosets $aW_J$ are $\\{1,s_1\\}$, $s_2W_J=\\{s_2,s_2s_1\\}$ and $s_1s_2W_J=\\{s_1s_2,s_1s_2s_1\\}$, again disjoint and exhausting $W$ by [F4]; their minimal elements are $1$ (length $0$), $s_2$ (length $1$, versus $\\ell(s_2s_1)=2$) and $s_1s_2$ (length $2$, versus $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3$), unique by the right-coset half of [F1]. For these three elements $d$ the right-handed additivity of [F1] gives $\\ell(ds_1)=\\ell(d)+\\ell(s_1)=\\ell(d)+1$, namely $\\ell(s_1)=1$, $\\ell(s_2s_1)=2=1+1$ and $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3=2+1$, as asserted; equivalently the right coset representatives satisfy the characterisation $\\ell(ds_1)>\\ell(d)$ of [F1].",
     "step": "1.2",
     "inputs": [
      "F4",
      "F1",
      "F3"
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "2.1",
     "claim": "**The left cosets and their minimal elements.** By [F4] the left cosets of $W_J=\\{1,s_1\\}$ are the sets $W_Ja=\\{ua:u\\in W_J\\}$ for $a\\in W$, and using the six-element list of [F3] they are $W_J\\cdot1=\\{1,s_1\\}$, $W_Js_2=\\{s_2,s_1s_2\\}$ and $W_Js_2s_1=\\{s_2s_1,s_1s_2s_1\\}$, which are disjoint and exhaust $W$. Reading the lengths off [F3], the minimum of $\\ell$ is $0$ on $\\{1,s_1\\}$ (attained at $1$), $1$ on $\\{s_2,s_1s_2\\}$ (attained at $s_2$) and $2$ on $\\{s_2s_1,s_1s_2s_1\\}$ (attained at $s_2s_1$); by [F1] each coset has a unique element of minimal length, so the minimal representatives are $1$, $s_2$ and $s_2s_1$ with lengths $0$, $1$ and $2$.",
     "step": "2.1",
     "inputs": [
      "F4",
      "F3",
      "F1",
      "1.1"
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "3.1",
     "claim": "**The descent characterisation and length additivity.** For the three minimal representatives $d=1$, $d=s_2$ and $d=s_2s_1$, the table of [F3] gives $\\ell(s_1\\cdot1)=\\ell(s_1)=1>0=\\ell(1)$, $\\ell(s_1s_2)=2>1=\\ell(s_2)$ and $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3>2=\\ell(s_2s_1)$, so each of them satisfies the characterisation $\\ell(s_1d)>\\ell(d)$ of [F1]. The additivity identity of [F1] for $u=s_1\\in W_J$ reads $\\ell(s_1d)=\\ell(s_1)+\\ell(d)$ for the minimal $d$; at $d=s_2$ this is $\\ell(s_1s_2)=1+1=2$ and at $d=s_2s_1$ it is $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=1+2=3$, the two values asserted in the statement.",
     "step": "3.1",
     "inputs": [
      "F3",
      "F1",
      "2.1"
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "4.1",
     "claim": "**Collected.** The example enumerates the three left cosets and the three right cosets of $W_J=\\{1,s_1\\}$ in $W\\cong S_3$, identifies their unique minimal representatives with the lengths predicted by the parabolic theorem, verifies the descent characterisations on both sides and the length-additivity identities $\\ell(ud)=\\ell(u)+\\ell(d)$ and $\\ell(du)=\\ell(d)+\\ell(u)$ for $u=s_1$ (steps 2.1, 3.1, 1.2).",
     "step": "4.1",
     "inputs": [
      "2.1",
      "3.1",
      "1.2",
      "1.1"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "routine_steps": [],
   "boundaries": [
    {
     "case": "empty",
     "status": "checked",
     "evidence": "No coset is empty and the three left cosets are pairwise disjoint and exhaust $W$ (step 2.1); the case of an empty index set does not occur since $J=\\{s_1\\}$."
    },
    {
     "case": "zero",
     "status": "checked",
     "evidence": "The identity has length $0$ and is the minimal representative of $W_J\\cdot1$ (steps 2.1 and 1.2 for the right cosets)."
    },
    {
     "case": "one",
     "status": "checked",
     "evidence": "The parabolic subgroup has one nonidentity element $u=s_1$, and the additivity identity is verified at that single value of $u$ (step 3.1)."
    },
    {
     "case": "degenerate",
     "status": "not_applicable",
     "reason": "No degenerate case arises: the six elements of $S_3$ and all three cosets on each side are enumerated, and $W_J$ has order $2$ throughout."
    },
    {
     "case": "endpoints",
     "status": "checked",
     "evidence": "The endpoint representatives, $1$ of length $0$ and the elements of maximal length $3$ in the cosets of $s_1s_2s_1$, are included in steps 2.1 and 1.2."
    },
    {
     "case": "nonempty-choice",
     "status": "checked",
     "evidence": "No Choice is used: the minimal representatives are unique by the theorem, and their lengths are read off a finite table (steps 2.1, 1.2)."
    },
    {
     "case": "iff-forward",
     "status": "checked",
     "evidence": "Forward direction of the descent characterization: the minimal representatives $1$, $s_2$, $s_2s_1$ satisfy $\\ell(s_1d)>\\ell(d)$ (step 3.1)."
    },
    {
     "case": "iff-reverse",
     "status": "checked",
     "evidence": "Reverse direction: the right-coset representatives $1$, $s_2$, $s_1s_2$ satisfy $\\ell(ds_1)=\\ell(d)+1>\\ell(d)$, exhibiting the converse descent-minimality implication (step 1.2)."
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}

