    "lem-hh-commuting-left-right-hecke-length-operators": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-hh-coxeter-exchange-deletion-and-faithfulness",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "**Exchange.** Let $w=s_1\\cdots s_k$ be a reduced expression and let $s\\in S$ satisfy $\\ell(sw)=k-1$. Then $$sw=s_1\\cdots\\widehat{s_i}\\cdots s_k$$ for some $i\\in\\{1,\\dots,k\\}$; equivalently, $w$ has a reduced expression beginning with $s$, and $s$ is a prefix reflection of any reduced expression of $w$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "1.3",
            "1.4",
            "1.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-free-module-on-a-set-and-standard-basis",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "More generally, a family $(b_x)_{x\\in X}$ is a **basis** of a module $M$ when every element of $M$ is uniquely a finite $R$-linear combination of the $b_x$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-hh-universal-coxeter-hecke-parameters-and-presentation",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**Generator conjugacy.** Two simple generators $s,t\\in S$ are conjugate in $W$ if and only if $s\\sim t$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-hh-dihedral-root-recurrence-and-root-sign",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "**Ambient reducedness of dihedral words.** Let $s\\ne t$, $m:=m(s,t)$, and for $q\\ge1$ let $w_q$ be the value of the alternating word of length $q$ beginning with $s$. If $m<\\infty$ and $q\\le m$, or if $m=\\infty$ and $q\\ge1$, then $\\ell(w_q)=q$",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-hh-matsumoto-reduced-word-theorem",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "**Braid moves.** Call two words in $S$ *braid-equivalent* when one is obtained from the other by finitely many replacements of an alternating subword $s\\,t\\,s\\,t\\cdots$ of length $m(s,t)<\\infty$ by the alternating word $t\\,s\\,t\\,s\\cdots$ of the same length. Then any two reduced expressions of the same element $w\\in W$ are braid-equivalent.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**The presented group.** Let $R\\subseteq F(S)$ be the set of relators $$R:=\\{s^2:s\\in S\\}\\cup\\{(st)^{m(s,t)}:s,t\\in S,\\ m(s,t)<\\infty\\},$$ where $F(S)$ is the free group on $S$ ([[def-free-group]], [[thm-reduced-words-form-the-free-group]]) and $(st)^k$ is the $k$-fold product ([[def-group-power]]), and let $N:=\\langle\\!\\langle R\\rangle\\!\\rangle_{F(S)}$ be the normal closure of $R$ in $F(S)$ ([[def-normal-closure]], [[prop-normal-closure-is-products-of-conjugates]]). Define $$W:=F(S)/N,$$ and write $s$ (as well as $sN$) for the image of $s\\in S$ in $W$",
          "uses": [
            "1.5",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "def-free-module-on-a-set-and-standard-basis",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Every element has a unique expression $$\\sum_{x\\in F}r_xe_x$$ with $F\\subseteq X$ finite.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "1.5",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "def-endomorphism-ring-of-a-module",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a left $R$-module $M$, define $$\\operatorname{End}_R(M):=\\operatorname{Hom}_R(M,M).$$ Addition is pointwise and multiplication is composition, $(fg)(m):=f(g(m))$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "def-module-homomorphism-kernel-image-and-cokernel",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For left $R$-modules $M,N$, a function $f:M\\to N$ is an **$R$-module homomorphism** if $$f(m+m')=f(m)+f(m')\\quad\\text{and}\\quad f(rm)=rf(m)$$ for all $m,m'\\in M$ and $r\\in R$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "d-1.1",
          "claim": "1.1 For $x\\in W$ and $s\\in S$, [F1] gives $\\ell(sx)=\\ell(x)\\pm1$, so exactly one clause of the displayed definition of $P_s$ applies to $e_x$, and likewise exactly one clause of the definition of $Q_s$ applies to $e_x$;",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "F1",
            "F6",
            "F7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1.2",
          "claim": "1.2 Write $u_s:=v_s-v_s^{-1}$.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "1.2",
            "F1",
            "F6",
            "F7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1.3",
          "claim": "1.3 (two-length lemma) Let $x\\in W$ and $s,t\\in S$ satisfy $\\ell(sxt)=\\ell(x)$ and $\\ell(sx)=\\ell(xt)$;",
          "step": "1.3",
          "inputs": [
            "1.3",
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1.4",
          "claim": "1.4 Fix $s,t\\in S$ and $x\\in W$ and expand both $P_sQ_t(e_x)$ and $Q_tP_s(e_x)$ from the definitions.",
          "step": "1.4",
          "inputs": [
            "1.4",
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1.5",
          "claim": "1.5 (reduced products at $e_1$) Let $w=s_1\\cdots s_k$ be a reduced expression and put $w_i:=s_1\\cdots s_i$ for $0\\le i\\le k$.",
          "step": "1.5",
          "inputs": [
            "1.5",
            "F1",
            "F5",
            "F6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-2.1",
          "claim": "2.1 In the two remaining length configurations, (v) $\\ell(sx)=\\ell(xt)=\\ell(x)-1$, $\\ell(sxt)=\\ell(x)$, the two expansions are $P_sQ_t(e_x)=e_{sxt}+u_te_{sx}+u_su_te_x$ and $Q_tP_s(e_x)=e_{sxt}+u_se_{xt}+u_su_te_x$;",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
